## NOTE — ACTIVE (design/proof pass); workable NOW, parallel with ADR-0015 / WCI-MVP

This is a **DESIGN/PROOF pass**, run the same way `DSGN-WCI-reshape.md` was: a manager design
sub-session drafts the contract, an **adversarial review** refutes it, then **operator
sign-off**. Its output is an **approved proof contract** — a specification, not code.

It is **INDEPENDENT of WCI-MVP being built** (`depends_on:` empty), so it runs in **parallel**
with the ADR-0015 → WCI-MVP engine track right now. The §5.1 proof reasons about
import/symbol/config/test coupling — it needs no in-flight engine code to be specified.

Why it matters: per `DSGN-WCI-reshape.md` §5 (open question 1, "highest risk") and §7.1 (the
F1 invariant), **nothing slices concurrently without this proof** — "the split is invented by
the proof, never by the label." The proof must be STRICTLY STRONGER than disjoint `owns` (B1:
path-disjointness proves nothing about imports/calls/shared state/config).

Its approved output is a **prerequisite for `WCI-FOLLOWON`** (the auto-slice / `merge_after`
concurrency payoff). WCI-FOLLOWON needs BOTH: WCI-MVP landed AND this proof approved.

Activation / done checklist:
1. Manager design sub-session drafts the §5.1 contract (signals + combine rule + conservative
   default + how `claimable` consumes the certificate deterministically).
2. Adversarial review (read-only, instructed to REFUTE) + synthesize.
3. Operator sign-off → APPROVED proof contract.
